 0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px; fon
 t-size: 13px;">[1] Singularity Engine: Dynamic JIT Java Compiler</h4>
 <p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">The m
 odel compiles and executes raw Java code directly inside your running
  NetBeans JVM utilizing our custom child-first ClassLoader. Build, te
 st, and hot-load live tools, Java swing panels, or complex dependency
  algorithms on-the-fly.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.uno/screensho
 ts/netbeans/NbJava.png" target="_blank"><img src="https://asi.anahata
 .uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/NbJava.png" alt="[1] Singularity Eng
 ine: Dynamic JIT Java Compiler" width="650" border="0" /></a></div><d
 iv style="margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; borde
 r: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; marg
 in-bottom: 6px; font-size: 13px;">[2] Multimodal Vision: Real-Time Sc
 reen & Region Sharing</h4><p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; 
 margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Share physical screens, specific monitors, or cu
 stom rectangular regions with the ASI. Perfect for providing real-tim
 e visual feedback on Swing UI renders, layouts, or compiler states.</
 p><a href="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/NetBeansLiveS
