 px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 
 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 
 13px;">[5] Agentic Feedback: Inline AI Code Annotations</h4><p style=
 "font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Model suggesti
 ons, code explanations, and diagnostics are painted dynamically direc
 tly onto your source code lines within the NetBeans editor, acting as
  non-intrusive guide markers.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.uno/scr
 eenshots/netbeans/InlineAIAnnotations.png" target="_blank"><img src="
 https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/InlineAIAnnotatio
 ns.png" alt="[5] Agentic Feedback: Inline AI Code Annotations" width=
 "650" border="0" /></a></div><div style="margin-bottom: 20px; padding
 : 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 style="colo
 r: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 13px;">[6] 
 Self-Healing Filesystem tracking (NbHandle)</h4><p style="font-size: 
 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Every resource handle in c
 ontext is bound to a native NetBeans FileObject. If you drag-and-drop
 , rename, cut, or paste a file across projects, the handle auto-heals
  and preserves context.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.uno/screensho
 ts/netbeans/NbHandleForFileObjectIntegration.png" target="_blank"><im
 g src="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/NbHandleFo
